( '2.1', 'CASE 2.1.11', 'Petra''s dining table commission', 'Consider petra pays carpenter Fabian 650 euros for an oak dining table he builds and delivers. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Petra''s family acts as a household and Fabian acts as an entrepreneur in this transaction.', 'The finished dining table is a good because it is a tangible item Fabian produces and delivers.', 'Paying for the table fulfils the family''s need for furniture through exchange.', 'Fabian has no genuine need for timber because raw materials are merely wants for any business.', 'Timber is a limited resource, so Fabian must economise on how much oak he uses per commission.'], ARRAY[true, true, true, false, true], ARRAY['TRUE — Households are consuming units that buy goods and services and may also sell labour or used items. Entrepreneurs organise production and sale under uncertainty. The same person can act as entrepreneur at work and as a household when shopping.

