( '2.1', 'CASE 2.1.31', 'Households and Entrepreneurs in Exchange', 'Analyze how households and entrepreneurs interact when goods and services change hands. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['A family selling a used bicycle online remains a household even while acting as a seller.', 'Exchange requires identical needs on both sides before any trade can occur.', 'Only multinational corporations count as entrepreneurs under basic economic definitions.', 'Households supply finished goods to entrepreneurs while firms supply only unpaid advice.', 'Repair workshops are households because customers visit the premises in person.'], ARRAY[true, false, false, false, false], ARRAY['TRUE — Households are consuming units that buy goods and services and may also sell labour or used items. Entrepreneurs organise production and sale under uncertainty. The same person can act as entrepreneur at work and as a household when shopping.

